WEBVTT

00:12.350 --> 00:13.630
At last...

00:13.630 --> 00:16.240
At last, the dark lord is defeated!

00:41.240 --> 00:43.780
You've done it, Sunraku!

00:43.780 --> 00:45.270
Thank you!

00:46.740 --> 00:50.370
It's been such a long, 
hard journey, hasn't it?

00:50.370 --> 00:51.590
Yes.

00:53.540 --> 00:56.070
I've been waiting so long 
for this very moment...

00:56.560 --> 00:57.410
Faeria.

01:04.460 --> 01:06.850
Now, you can go with the dark lord

01:06.850 --> 01:10.500
straight to hell!

01:21.600 --> 01:23.720
You're the real dark lord here!

01:23.720 --> 01:26.310
You're the real menace to the world!

01:26.310 --> 01:28.810
~The Prayer of the Fairy Princess~

01:29.070 --> 01:30.660
Heck yeah!

01:30.660 --> 01:33.320
I finally beat <i>Failia Chronicle</i>!

01:34.070 --> 01:37.330
And I got my revenge 
for everything she put me through!

01:37.330 --> 01:38.520
Yeah!

01:39.080 --> 01:42.060
<i>In an age where display-based 
games are considered retro,</i>

01:42.060 --> 01:45.440
<i>and fully immersive VR games 
have become the norm...</i>

01:42.990 --> 01:46.040
Simulated Environment

01:46.040 --> 01:48.070
<i>Beneath the small number 
of works of significance</i>

01:48.070 --> 01:50.480
<i>lies a massive pile of releases</i>

01:50.480 --> 01:55.670
<i>whose game designs don't live up 
to their improved graphics technology.</i>

01:56.260 --> 01:59.400
<i>They are known as "trash games."</i>

01:59.720 --> 02:02.260
Not Trash Games

01:59.720 --> 02:06.730
Semi-Redeemable Trash Games

02:00.100 --> 02:04.230
<i>Although most people 
rightfully despise trash games,</i>

02:01.550 --> 02:06.730
Never Play Again

02:04.230 --> 02:06.730
<i>there are those who gleefully seek them out.</i>

02:06.980 --> 02:09.640
<i>We call these people "freaks."</i>

02:09.640 --> 02:13.610
The rumors were true. 
What a giant pile of garbage!

02:18.990 --> 02:20.800
<i>This man here, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

02:20.800 --> 02:23.600
<i>is one of these freaks.</i>

02:20.950 --> 02:24.200
<b>Rakuro Hizutome</b>

02:21.130 --> 02:24.290
<b>High School 2nd-Year</b>

02:24.700 --> 02:26.950
I feel so free!

02:27.430 --> 02:31.450
Is this how a convict finishing up 
a prison sentence feels?

02:32.380 --> 02:35.950
Now, what trash game will I try next?

02:36.500 --> 02:39.540
<i>He is known as the "Trash-Game Hunter."</i>

04:10.310 --> 04:14.480
<b>What Do You Play Games For?</b>

04:12.120 --> 04:14.040
Morning!

04:15.730 --> 04:17.360
Oh, no one's here.

04:19.860 --> 04:22.110
<b>Soft & Fluffy Melon Pan</b>

04:19.860 --> 04:25.110
<b>Kuon Amane</b>

04:19.860 --> 04:25.110
The Celebrity Model on Fashion's Bleeding Edge

04:27.300 --> 04:30.700
Mom, one of your butterflies got out.

04:30.700 --> 04:33.250
Oh, drat! Thanks for telling me!

04:33.650 --> 04:35.240
Heading out!

04:36.580 --> 04:38.120
Have a good day!

04:40.880 --> 04:42.720
Where're you going for summer break?

04:42.720 --> 04:44.460
Heading to Hawaii in two days!

04:44.460 --> 04:45.690
Awesome!

04:45.690 --> 04:46.300
You?

04:46.300 --> 04:47.370
Makihari.

04:46.300 --> 04:50.310
<b>Municipal
Mahinoki
High School</b>

04:47.370 --> 04:48.260
Going to the game expo?

04:48.260 --> 04:49.990
Hey, great idea!

05:00.260 --> 05:02.980
E-Excuse me... Hizutome-kun...

05:03.570 --> 05:06.270
Wh-What have you been up to?

05:06.740 --> 05:07.950
Th-That's not what I meant!

05:07.950 --> 05:11.580
I meant to ask... what game are you playing?

05:12.440 --> 05:15.210
Oh, really? The truth is, I also—

05:19.080 --> 05:20.180
Okay!

05:30.680 --> 05:31.390
Hizu—

05:31.390 --> 05:32.590
'Sup, Rakuro?

05:32.590 --> 05:33.430
Heya.

05:33.430 --> 05:35.090
Up all night gaming again?

05:35.090 --> 05:36.750
As a matter of fact...

05:36.750 --> 05:40.120
Listen to this, man! 
Talk about a nightmare...

05:40.120 --> 05:42.690
Trashiest trash game ever...

05:52.840 --> 05:54.790
Summer vacation starts tomorrow, then?

05:55.580 --> 05:59.830
<b>Mana Iwamaki</b>

05:55.760 --> 05:59.830
<b>Owner of "Rock Roll"</b>

05:56.790 --> 05:58.780
That should bring in some business, I'll bet.

06:01.420 --> 06:02.400
Come on in!

06:02.400 --> 06:03.960
Oh, Rei-chan!

06:05.570 --> 06:06.830
Hello, there!

06:06.970 --> 06:08.930
<b>Rei Saiga</b>

06:07.150 --> 06:08.930
<b>High School 2nd-Year</b>

06:08.930 --> 06:10.430
On the way back from practice?

06:10.430 --> 06:11.420
Yes.

06:15.060 --> 06:18.060
Sorry, but he's not here today, either.

06:18.730 --> 06:21.160
O-Oh, I just came to look at the games—

06:21.160 --> 06:24.310
C'mon, I know you too well 
for that little act.

06:22.440 --> 06:25.440
<b>BLUSH</b>

06:25.440 --> 06:27.760
Aw, you lucky girl!

06:27.760 --> 06:29.320
Oh, to be young and in love!

06:29.320 --> 06:31.310
M-Mana-san!

06:31.310 --> 06:34.830
He's been trying to crack 
an extra-special trash game,

06:34.830 --> 06:37.040
so he hasn't been by in a while.

06:37.390 --> 06:38.970
"Extra-special"?

06:38.970 --> 06:40.790
That one there's his latest.

06:40.790 --> 06:42.830
<i>Failia Chronicle</i>.

06:42.830 --> 06:44.710
It might take him a bit longer yet.

06:44.710 --> 06:47.930
Oh, <i>Faeria Chronicle Online</i>...

06:47.930 --> 06:49.890
My sister told me about that one.

06:49.890 --> 06:51.800
She said it was really hard!

06:51.800 --> 06:54.360
It's a legendary trash game.

06:54.360 --> 06:56.680
Miserable ally AI,

06:56.680 --> 06:59.350
utterly absurd enemy attack patterns,

06:59.350 --> 07:02.110
and more bugs in the code 
than you can shake a stick at.

07:02.990 --> 07:06.780
I hear you need serious skills 
to even beat the first boss.

07:06.780 --> 07:10.700
It's caused tons of players to 
throw their headsets in frustration!

07:10.700 --> 07:12.690
On top of that, I've heard

07:12.690 --> 07:16.080
you gotta fight the final boss 
in board shorts and a mask!

07:16.440 --> 07:18.130
Why in the world would you do that?

07:18.130 --> 07:19.100
No idea.

07:19.100 --> 07:22.180
I assume it's an efficiency 
thing or something.

07:22.730 --> 07:24.460
So? Are you making progress, Rei-chan?

07:25.070 --> 07:27.340
Yes. I am, but—

07:28.770 --> 07:31.720
Got any decent trash games in?

07:32.080 --> 07:34.550
Hey! Been a while, Hizutome-kun!

07:35.130 --> 07:35.950
Oh?

07:36.320 --> 07:37.810
And... she's gone.

07:39.270 --> 07:41.320
Oh, nothing.

07:41.320 --> 07:44.020
Wait, did you beat <i>Failia</i> already?

07:44.340 --> 07:45.620
You bet!

07:45.620 --> 07:47.320
I took that sucker down!

07:47.320 --> 07:48.550
How was it?

07:48.550 --> 07:51.810
It was a <i>spectacular</i> pile of garbage!

07:51.810 --> 07:53.610
Glad to hear it.

07:53.610 --> 07:56.490
The biggest pile of garbage 
was that female lead.

07:56.490 --> 07:59.500
Her name's "Faeria," 
and she ticked me off to no end!

07:59.910 --> 08:02.870
She's the cause of pretty much every 
problem you run into on the journey,

08:02.870 --> 08:06.920
and then she makes the situation worse and 
gets villagers and party members killed!

08:06.920 --> 08:08.000
<b>Tee-hee</b>

08:09.190 --> 08:11.120
Oh, no! I hit him!

08:11.120 --> 08:12.870
What the hell is your problem?!

08:12.870 --> 08:15.840
What are you even doing in that carriage?!

08:12.870 --> 08:15.840
And if you expect her to suffer 
consequences for any of it...

08:15.840 --> 08:17.350
Curse you, dark lord!

08:17.350 --> 08:20.460
He's the reason all of this is happening!

08:22.190 --> 08:25.440
She always finds a way to 
blame it all on the last boss!

08:25.440 --> 08:26.770
That guy didn't do squat!

08:26.770 --> 08:28.150
You're the real problem here!

08:28.600 --> 08:30.310
The same thing happens anywhere you go,

08:30.310 --> 08:32.650
but if you give her even the tiniest 
little shove to vent your annoyance...

08:33.160 --> 08:34.310
Now I'm mad!

08:34.310 --> 08:36.350
I'm not going anywhere with you!

08:36.660 --> 08:37.410
<b>Huh?!</b>

08:37.410 --> 08:39.610
She refuses to move the story along!

08:39.610 --> 08:41.320
The autosave locks you 
into that state of affairs,

08:41.320 --> 08:43.460
and it takes three freaking hours 
to get back in her good graces!

08:43.460 --> 08:46.240
Then there's this, that, 
and the other thing...

08:46.240 --> 08:48.680
Just thinking about it ticks me off again!

08:49.140 --> 08:51.550
I'm impressed you didn't throw in the towel.

08:51.550 --> 08:53.370
Oh, but you see, that's how they get you!

08:53.370 --> 08:57.270
In the three minutes between beating the final 
boss and before the credits start rolling,

08:57.270 --> 08:59.290
I guess because it's technically a cutscene,

08:59.290 --> 09:02.810
you can beat the crap out of Faeria 
without fear of reprisal!

09:03.150 --> 09:06.080
It's so ironic. The more Faeria annoys you,

09:06.080 --> 09:08.180
the more determined you 
become to brave that hell

09:08.180 --> 09:11.140
to experience that three minutes of heaven.

09:11.520 --> 09:14.290
But when that moment finally arrives...

09:15.580 --> 09:18.360
It's as if all that's wiped away!

09:18.360 --> 09:20.530
You feel like you understand 
why you were put on this Earth.

09:20.530 --> 09:22.570
Glad to hear you had fun.

09:22.570 --> 09:26.670
But since <i>Failia</i> turned out to be 
such a remarkable trash pile,

09:26.670 --> 09:29.210
I can't think of what to follow it up with.

09:32.960 --> 09:34.820
In that case,

09:34.820 --> 09:37.040
why not play something that's 
not a trash game for once?

09:37.460 --> 09:39.010
Not a trash game?

09:39.010 --> 09:45.020
<b>Summer Break Promotion!!
Now Adding Servers!</b>

09:39.810 --> 09:43.750
Experiencing the lows in life 
can help you appreciate the highs.

09:43.750 --> 09:45.540
The reverse is true, as well.

09:45.890 --> 09:50.340
The fully immersive VR game 
with over 30 million players...

09:53.170 --> 09:55.860
<i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>?

10:01.020 --> 10:05.120
It can be fun to try things designed 
for mass appeal now and then.

10:05.560 --> 10:06.330
Right?

10:09.070 --> 10:10.940
The opposite of a trash game...

10:11.530 --> 10:14.520
A real god-tier game, huh?

10:20.740 --> 10:24.530
<i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>, AKA SLF.

10:24.530 --> 10:27.340
It went on the market last spring

10:27.340 --> 10:32.140
and set a Guinness World Record 
for simultaneous player log-ins.

10:35.550 --> 10:37.320
The concept is...

10:37.970 --> 10:41.080
A colony fleet that came from space died out,

10:41.080 --> 10:44.630
but not before leaving a new society behind.

10:44.630 --> 10:46.960
Thousands of years later,

10:46.960 --> 10:53.030
the PCs are living their lives 
at roughly medieval tech levels.

10:53.030 --> 10:56.340
A setup that allows for effortless 
inclusion of sci-fi elements...

10:56.660 --> 10:58.380
Unlike <i>Failia</i>, which is so bad

10:58.380 --> 11:01.430
the haters find themselves desperately 
searching for redeeming features,

11:01.980 --> 11:04.330
this game is so beloved that its few haters

11:04.330 --> 11:06.930
are completely drowned out 
by tens of thousands of fans.

11:25.600 --> 11:28.330
<i>Utopia Entertainment Software.</i>

11:28.330 --> 11:30.820
<i>"UES" for short.</i>

11:30.820 --> 11:34.110
<i>Founded by the genius 
programmer Tsukuyo Tsukuri,</i>

11:34.110 --> 11:37.760
<i>who developed the fully 
immersive VR game system,</i>

11:37.760 --> 11:40.640
<i>it's a leader in the fields 
of software development,</i>

11:40.640 --> 11:43.180
<i>hardware, and Internet service provision.</i>

11:44.010 --> 11:47.550
If <i>SLF</i> was produced in-house at UES,

11:47.550 --> 11:49.930
there's no way it can be bad.

11:50.620 --> 11:53.970
How long's it been since I played 
something that wasn't a trash game?

11:59.010 --> 12:01.180
I did log in, right?

