 Pioneers, Feel the Night Wind</b>

14:44.110 --> 14:45.220
A forest?

15:00.450 --> 15:01.980
Awesome!

15:01.980 --> 15:04.940
Moving around feels 
pretty much like real life!

15:10.990 --> 15:12.230
I can run!

15:12.930 --> 15:14.300
I can grab!

15:14.300 --> 15:15.310
I can climb!

15:18.950 --> 15:22.000
<i>Failia</i> was so awkward to move around in...

15:22.340 --> 15:24.910
Actually, it feels like 
an insult to compare them.

15:26.510 --> 15:29.540
Whoa! It's huge!

15:37.650 --> 15:40.250
So this is the world of <i>SLF</i>...

15:45.920 --> 15:48.410
So... where am I, exactly?

15:48.410 --> 15:54.120
Don't games like these usually start you 
off in a tutorial town for beginners?

15:54.500 --> 15:56.270
<i>What Sunraku didn't realize</i>

15:56.270 --> 15:59.270
<i>is that those who choose 
"Wanderer" as their origin</i>

15:59.270 --> 16:04.270
<i>will start out at a random 
point in the beginners' area.</i>

16:04.270 --> 16:15.990
The Rampant Forest

16:04.270 --> 16:15.990
<i><b>Sunraku</b></i>

16:04.270 --> 16:15.990
Firstia

16:04.290 --> 16:07.610
This starter map looks pretty basic.

16:07.930 --> 16:09.560
Let's see...

16:09.560 --> 16:12.550
This is "The Rampant Forest,"

16:12.550 --> 16:15.730
and to the west is 
the starting town, "Firstia."

16:18.910 --> 16:20.170
Guess that's it.

16:20.170 --> 16:23.160
Okay, I'll head roughly in that 
direction while I check things out!

16:27.890 --> 16:30.180
I can even land properly!

16:30.180 --> 16:32.610
I know this stuff should go without saying,

16:32.610 --> 16:35.090
but actually getting to 
play it feels so good!

16:36.140 --> 16:41.600
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

16:36.140 --> 16:41.600
Mercenary (Twin Blade User) Skill Points Remaining: 0

16:36.140 --> 16:41.600
Cash on Hand  9000 Mahni

16:36.140 --> 16:41.600
HP: 30
 Stamina: 20
 Strength: 10 
 Dexterity:15 
 Vitality: 3

16:36.140 --> 16:41.600
Magic: 10 
 Agility: 10
 Tech: 15 
 Luck: 30

16:36.690 --> 16:38.440
Vitality: 3.

16:38.440 --> 16:41.600
Figures I'd have low defense with 
the half-naked thing going on...

16:41.600 --> 16:46.090
We'll have to see how far 
that high luck stat gets me.

16:55.130 --> 16:57.160
Right as I start playing?!

16:58.470 --> 17:00.040
A Goblin, huh?

17:00.630 --> 17:02.100
In that case...

17:02.700 --> 17:06.750
Let's see what this combat engine's made of!

17:05.460 --> 17:06.750
<b>Mercenary Twinblade</b>

17:28.230 --> 17:30.210
Wow, a one-hit kill?

17:30.210 --> 17:32.300
But it's just a scrub enemy 
in the intro, I guess.

17:32.810 --> 17:35.070
Hey, I leveled up!

17:35.070 --> 17:37.860
<b>Dropped Item 
 Goblin Hand Axe</b>

17:38.170 --> 17:41.060
Says it can be dual-wielded, 
so it's an option...

17:41.500 --> 17:44.020
But its durability is already down to half.

17:44.020 --> 17:46.370
Probably won't last much longer, then.

17:51.210 --> 17:55.390
<i>Monster weaknesses, 
patterns, and item drops...</i>

17:55.390 --> 17:57.640
<i>There's a lot to learn here.</i>

17:57.970 --> 18:02.010
<i>Trash game or god-tier game, you 
get this feeling everywhere...</i>

18:02.970 --> 18:06.450
<i>The elation of diving 
head-first into a new world...</i>

18:06.450 --> 18:09.170
<i>You just can't get that in real life!</i>

18:10.230 --> 18:13.900
Okay, let's not forget to enjoy this!

18:30.220 --> 18:32.090
Well, would you look at that?

18:32.730 --> 18:34.630
One hit from that could put me down.

18:34.340 --> 18:35.840
<b>Vorpal Bunny</b>

18:54.020 --> 18:56.530
One critical won't do it for this one, huh?!

19:02.880 --> 19:05.030
Is this all you've got, god-tier game?

19:05.790 --> 19:08.350
If you go for the neck 
with every single pass,

19:08.350 --> 19:10.040
I'm gonna figure out what you're doing.

19:13.110 --> 19:14.390
Look at all that EXP!

19:14.390 --> 19:16.410
He was a tough little guy, huh?

19:17.160 --> 19:19.090
No weapon drops, though, huh?

19:19.090 --> 19:22.840
I wanted that knife! 
I bet it's powerful as heck!

19:23.300 --> 19:26.310
Condition Achieved

19:23.300 --> 19:26.310
You Learned
<b>Flash Counter</b>

19:24.810 --> 19:26.310
"Condition Achieved"?

19:27.090 --> 19:29.810
I can learn skills by taking 
certain actions, huh?

19:29.810 --> 19:34.060
<b>New Skill</b>

19:29.810 --> 19:34.060
<b>Flash Counter</b>

19:29.810 --> 19:34.060
Bonus added to counters from parry.

19:29.810 --> 19:34.060
<b>Parry: Deflecting an attack with your weapon</b>

19:30.730 --> 19:33.420
Hey, yeah, I haven't used any skills yet...

19:34.070 --> 19:36.770
This game's pretty well designed.

19:37.230 --> 19:40.710
Since a player's own skill 
supplements your dodges and parries,

19:40.710 --> 19:43.660
I can fight pretty well against 
even higher-level enemies.

19:44.110 --> 19:47.950
That makes me wanna try a bunch 
of different fighting styles!

19:48.330 --> 19:49.110
Hang on!

19:49.110 --> 19:52.210
Have I been played this whole time 
without encountering a single bug?!

19:52.210 --> 19:55.380
<b>Invisibility Bug</b>

19:52.210 --> 19:55.380
What's going on? I can't see anything!

19:55.380 --> 19:57.630
<b>Clipping Bug</b>

19:55.380 --> 19:57.630
Hey, I found a hidden world!

19:57.630 --> 19:58.090
<b>Swish</b>

19:57.630 --> 20:00.130
<b>Hitbox Bug</b>

19:57.630 --> 20:00.130
Darn it! Why can't I hit you?!

19:58.130 --> 19:58.590
<b>Swish</b>

19:58.880 --> 19:59.340
<b>Swish</b>

19:59.380 --> 19:59.590
<b>Swish</b>

19:59.880 --> 20:00.090
<b>Swish</b>

20:00.580 --> 20:03.380
Awesome! That's a god-tier game for you!

20:04.510 --> 20:08.670
I honestly wasn't sure if I could enjoy 
a bug-free game after all this time,

20:08.670 --> 20:11.870
but I can really have a good time with this!

20:11.870 --> 20:15.150
I guess they don't call it 
"god-tier" for nothing!

20:15.610 --> 20:16.900
Okay!

20:16.900 --> 20:20.650
I'm gonna get me a tough 
bunny's kitchen knife!

20:20.650 --> 20:23.760
Where are you, bunny?!

20:27.780 --> 20:30.450
<b>Spin Slash
</b>A spinning slash area attack

20:39.630 --> 20:41.610
That skill's kinda crummy.

20:41.610 --> 20:43.780
The big flashy swing 
leaves me open for too long.

20:45.020 --> 20:46.700
Hey, finally leveled again.

20:47.010 --> 20:50.980
I should probably allocate 
my stat points already...

20:53.960 --> 20:59.400
I wish that Vorpal Bunny thing 
had a higher spawn rate, though...

20:55.230 --> 20:56.730
<b>Vorpal Bunny</b>

20:59.400 --> 21:01.480
Guess it was a rare enemy, huh?

21:01.980 --> 21:06.430
It took me forever to get 
a matching set of those knives!

21:04.820 --> 21:07.740
<b>Play Time</b>

21:09.090 --> 21:11.150
Since I beat about fifty of 'em...

21:11.150 --> 21:14.280
I guess that's a drop rate of about 5 percent or so?

21:13.830 --> 21:19.500
<b>Vorpal Chopper
</b>Bonus to critical damage.

21:14.600 --> 21:16.660
This thing's pretty darn rare, huh?

21:16.660 --> 21:19.290
They've got better stats 
than the Mercenary Twinblade,

21:19.290 --> 21:21.050
so I'd better take good care of 'em.

21:21.050 --> 21:26.840
Spin Slash 
 Flash Counter 
 Tap Step 
 Screw Pierce

21:21.490 --> 21:24.430
And I learned a few new skills...

21:24.430 --> 21:27.390
But Screw Pierce seems 
like the only useful one.

21:26.880 --> 21:30.470
<b>New Skill</b>

21:26.880 --> 21:30.470
<b>Screw Pierce</b>

21:26.880 --> 21:30.470
 Deals a quick strike with a compact weapon
 This attack is powerful but cannot be chained

21:27.390 --> 21:29.810
The others seem more 
"better than nothing" tier.

21:30.970 --> 21:35.790
Still, I'm not gonna gain any more levels 
with the scrub-tier monsters around here.

21:35.790 --> 21:37.600
I'd better move on.

21:38.020 --> 21:39.480
The Rampant Forest

21:38.020 --> 21:39.480
Firstia

21:38.750 --> 21:41.900
I've strayed pretty far away 
from the starting town, huh?

21:39.480 --> 21:40.730
The Rampant Forest

21:39.480 --> 21:40.730
Firstia

21:41.900 --> 21:46.070
At this point, I'm a lot closer 
to the next one, Secondale.

21:42.900 --> 21:46.900
Secondale

21:42.900 --> 21:46.900
<i><b>Sunraku</b></i>

21:46.520 --> 21:48.170
To get to Secondale...

21:48.170 --> 21:51.620
I've gotta cross this bridge 
over the ravine, huh?

22:01.090 --> 22:03.000
Aha, I see.

22:07.590 --> 22:11.740
I gotta beat you if 
I wanna cross. Is that it?

22:16.560 --> 22:17.520
Sounds good to me.

22:18.280 --> 22:21.020
Looks like I've got me 
a real challenge at last.

22:21.020 --> 22:30.910
<b>Ravenous Python</b>

22:21.020 --> 22:30.910
<b>Area Boss</b>

22:21.020 --> 22:30.910
Rec. Level:

22:21.020 --> 22:30.910
Rec. Party Size:

22:22.070 --> 22:25.310
Soloing a boss meant for a party, huh?

22:25.740 --> 22:28.290
With the great ratings <i>SLF</i> gets,

22:28.290 --> 22:30.910
it probably won't be dishing out 
any silly bug attacks.

22:30.910 --> 22:33.920
<i>A snake monster's attacks 
usually consist of...</i>

22:33.920 --> 22:36.910
<i>Coil, bite, tail swipe, swallow, venom...</i>

22:36.910 --> 22:38.220
<i>That should be all.</i>

22:38.580 --> 22:41.510
With an avatar that actually 
moves the way I want it to,

22:41.510 --> 22:43.340
I don't need defenses to beat you!

22:44.210 --> 22:45.840
Give me something to enjoy here,

22:47.490 --> 22:50.470
<i>SLF</i>!

23:24.420 --> 23:26.670
The Rampant Forest

23:42.600 --> 23:46.480
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:44.480 --> 23:49.190
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:46.480 --> 23:47.940
Mini!

23:52.730 --> 23:54.330
H-Hello, there!

23:54.330 --> 23:55.910
I'm Psyger-0!

23:55.910 --> 24:00.600
I'd like to show you the prologue text that 
rolls at the start of <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>,

24:00.600 --> 24:03.010
which Hizutome-kun skipped!

24:03.010 --> 24:04.710
Take it away!

24:07.710 --> 24:19.520
<b>The land is vast, and through it is woven the grand tapestry of life...
We, who live in the here and now, use the artifacts of the past
still breathing in history and ruins to trace the footsteps of the Divine.</b>

24:19.520 --> 24:31.280
<b>You are a pioneer, appearing with the wind from the east, and though
brought to your knees time and again, you brave ever onward...
And, like the wind, some of you will simply fade away.
What is the purpose of your life?</b>

24:31.280 --> 24:40.990
<b>Will you trust your life to the swing of your sword?
 Will you peer into the depths of the magical arts
and seek to master your craft?
 Or will you choose not to fight at all?
</b>

24:40.990 --> 24:50.580
<b>All options can be found here.
 All options exist within you.
Now, take your first step.
Explore the unknown, your future, and your potential.</b>

24:50.580 --> 24:58.720
<b>This is the mission given unto you,
the children of the Divinity born—fallen—upon this land.</b>

24:59.260 --> 25:01.070
Divine? Divinity?

25:01.070 --> 25:03.430
There's so much intriguing jargon, isn't there?

25:03.430 --> 25:05.550
Well, see you again soon!

25:05.550 --> 25:07.000
Bye-bye!

25:08.930 --> 25:12.800
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

25:10.530 --> 25:15.530
<b>SLF Mini</b>

25:12.800 --> 25:14.380
Mini!

25:17.050 --> 25:19.690
Oh, no! I hit him!

25:19.690 --> 25:21.190
What the hell is your problem?!

25:21.190 --> 25:23.080
What are you even doing in that carriage?!

25:23.080 --> 25:25.710
I told you to wait on the dang bench!

25:26.500 --> 25:27.580
<b>Tee-hee</b>

25:27.580 --> 25:29.100
Curse you, dark lord!

25:29.100 --> 25:31.990
He's the reason all of this is happening!

25:31.990 --> 25:33.420
But this is all your fault!

25:34.220 --> 25:35.300
<b>Tee-hee</b>

25:35.300 --> 25:36.710
Now I'm mad!

25:36.710 --> 25:38.470
I'm not going anywhere with you!

25:38.180 --> 25:42.810
<b>Huh?!</b>

25:38.470 --> 25:40.350
You're the one who causes all the problems,

25:40.350 --> 25:42.810
and I'm the one fighting, not you!

25:43.270 --> 25:44.350
<b>Tee-hee</b>
